Earthing, bonding, return paths and touch/step potentials (@pe-earthing: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @electrical-power-engineering, #source "../sources/Electrical-Installation-Guide-Schneider.lingua#r_045M70B905F19RA4E6FTNXFC0V", #source "../sources/Medium-Voltage-Technical-Guide-Schneider.lingua#r_77NSGJV2R4FM4513WTNWE456J2", #source "../sources/Electrical-Standards-Edition-and-Jurisdiction.lingua#r_169QEF26N0C345MKSRWQY6KD90", #source "../sources/NR-10-and-the-2026-Revision.lingua#r_4C6VMVCTGT5WCFYHEHC9TJ2W4X", #electrical-power-engineering "Insulation-coordination-surges-and-dielectric-condition.lingua#r_59ZVMCW67D4VKN4YNEJSPX0Z1Z") { r_2324AA0XT8K4G0A82TV2ABPK80
**Read:** [Electrical Installation Guide — Schneider Electric](../sources/Electrical-Installation-Guide-Schneider.lingua#r_045M70B905F19RA4E6FTNXFC0V), complete earthing/bonding and fault-protection sections; [Medium Voltage Technical Guide — Schneider Electric](../sources/Medium-Voltage-Technical-Guide-Schneider.lingua#r_77NSGJV2R4FM4513WTNWE456J2), whole applicable earth-fault and service-condition guidance; [Electrical standards, edition and jurisdiction](../sources/Electrical-Standards-Edition-and-Jurisdiction.lingua#r_169QEF26N0C345MKSRWQY6KD90), actual complete applicable installation/grounding requirements; [NR-10 — applicable text, revisions and dates](../sources/NR-10-and-the-2026-Revision.lingua#r_4C6VMVCTGT5WCFYHEHC9TJ2W4X), the complete text applicable at the place/date.

Earthing and bonding define physical fault/charge paths and potential relationships; earth is not a universal zero-impedance sink. Distinguish a circuit neutral, protective conductor, bonded structure, grounding electrode and a numerical reference node. Current returns through a complete source circuit with impedance and geometry.

For a documented installation, trace normal, leakage, lightning and fault paths separately. Compute relevant current and potential distributions with the actual source, soil/structure, conductor and connection model. A low electrode-resistance value alone does not establish acceptable touch/step exposure, protective-device operation or bonding continuity. Surface potential gradients, fault duration and the person's contact path matter.

Compare earthing arrangements and the associated fault-detection/clearing method through the actual applicable standard and equipment evidence. Include parallel paths, neutral earthing impedance, corrosion and changed topology. Physical testing and temporary protective-grounding work require qualified procedures; analyse a complete public case or suitable supervised setup and label the evidence honestly. This subject develops the model and reasoning needed to interpret such practice, rather than copying a generic grounding recipe into every system.

**Continue:** [Insulation coordination, surges and dielectric condition](Insulation-coordination-surges-and-dielectric-condition.lingua#r_59ZVMCW67D4VKN4YNEJSPX0Z1Z).

